YO is free to use. This licence explains what that means.

1. You may
   - download and install YO on any computer you own or use,
   - use it for free, for personal, study or work purposes,
   - share the official installer, unchanged, with other people, as long as you don't charge for it.

2. You may not
   - copy, change, translate, or build on YO's source code, design, artwork or its mascot,
   - take YO apart to get at its code (decompile, unpack or reverse engineer it), except where the law
     where you live allows it no matter what this licence says,
   - sell, rent or sublicense YO, or bundle it with something you sell,
   - publish YO, or a changed copy of it, under another name, or as if it were yours,
   - remove or hide this licence, the copyright notice, or the credits.

3. Other people's work
   YO is built with open-source software, such as Electron and Chromium. Those parts keep their own
   licences, which are included with YO (LICENSE.electron.txt and LICENSES.chromium.html in the
   installed folder). This licence doesn't change them.

4. Your data
   What you put in YO stays on your computer. YO has no account, no cloud and no tracking.
   PRIVACY.md (and "About YO" in the app) lists what YO keeps and what it sends.

5. No warranty
   YO is given "as is", without any warranty. The author is not responsible for any loss or damage
   that comes from using it, as far as the law allows. Keep backups of anything important; YO can
   make them for you (About YO, Your data).

6. Changes and ending
   A new version of YO may come with a new version of this licence. If you break this licence, your
   right to use YO ends.

